## Prepare service

Install dependencies:

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```
{% if use_grpc %}
### gRPC — generate protobuf stubs

Requires `grpc_tools` (`pip install grpcio-tools`):

```bash
make proto
```
{% endif %}
{% if use_sql %}
### Database migrations

Create a new migration (after adding/changing models):

```bash
make migration-create name=<your_migration_name>
```

Apply migrations:

```bash
make migration
```

Rollback last migration:

```bash
make migration-down
```
{% endif %}

## Run

```bash
make run
```

Endpoints after startup:
{% if use_rest %}
- **REST API** → `http://localhost:${HTTP_PORT:-8000}`
{% for module in modules %}  - `GET  /v1/{{ module | replace('_', '-') }}/`
  - `GET  /v1/{{ module | replace('_', '-') }}/{id}`
  - `POST /v1/{{ module | replace('_', '-') }}/`
  - `PUT  /v1/{{ module | replace('_', '-') }}/{id}`
  - `DELETE /v1/{{ module | replace('_', '-') }}/{id}`
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if use_graphql %}
- **GraphQL** → `http://localhost:${HTTP_PORT:-8000}/graphql` *(shared with REST if USE_REST=true, else port+100)*
{% endif %}
{% if use_grpc %}
- **gRPC** → `localhost:${GRPC_PORT:-8002}`
{% endif %}
{% if use_task_queue %}
- **Task Queue Dashboard** → `http://localhost:${TASK_QUEUE_DASHBOARD_PORT:-8080}`
{% endif %}

## Configuration

Copy and edit the environment file:

```bash
cp .env .env.local
```

Key variables:

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `HTTP_PORT` | `8000` | REST API port |
{% if use_grpc %}| `GRPC_PORT` | `8002` | gRPC port |
{% endif %}{% if use_task_queue %}| `TASK_QUEUE_DASHBOARD_PORT` | `8080` | Task queue dashboard port |
{% endif %}{% if use_sql %}| `SQL_DSN_WRITE` | — | PostgreSQL write DSN |
| `SQL_DSN_READ` | — | PostgreSQL read DSN (defaults to write) |
{% endif %}{% if use_redis %}| `REDIS_DSN_WRITE` | — | Redis DSN |
{% endif %}{% if use_mongo %}| `MONGO_DSN_WRITE` | — | MongoDB DSN |
{% endif %}{% if use_kafka %}| `KAFKA_BROKERS` | `localhost:9092` | Kafka broker(s) |
| `KAFKA_CONSUMER_GROUP` | `{{ package }}` | Kafka consumer group |
{% endif %}{% if use_rabbitmq %}| `RABBITMQ_BROKER` | `amqp://guest:guest@localhost:5672/` | RabbitMQ DSN |
{% endif %}| `MAX_WORKERS` | `10` | Per-worker concurrency cap |

